Project Documentation Phase
The Project Documentation Phase involves preparing a complete written record of the project. Documentation helps explain what the project is, why it was developed, how it works, and what technologies were used. The report can begin with the project title, introduction, problem statement, objectives, and proposed solution.
The documentation can then explain the requirements, system design, technologies, development process, and AI integration. The team can include diagrams such as a system architecture diagram or flowchart to explain the working process. Screenshots of the PocketSmart AI interface can also be included to show the different stages of user interaction.
The testing process and results are also recorded. The team can mention the different test cases used and whether the application produced the expected results. Any challenges faced during development and the solutions used to overcome them can also be included.
Finally, the documentation can contain the project conclusion and future scope. Possible future improvements could include additional expense categories, better visualization of spending, more personalized recommendations, and additional budgeting features. Proper documentation makes the project easier to understand, evaluate, and maintain.
